# Local configuration must never enter the build context. `.env` is gitignored, so
# `git status --porcelain` does not report it and the tree still measures clean --
# which means an image could carry uncommitted configuration or secrets while its
# provenance claimed an exact commit. Excluding it here makes the image right and
# the claim true for the same reason. Raised in review of #511.
# Every path git ignores is also kept out of the build context, unless it is
# deliberately packaged. `git status --porcelain` does not report ignored files, so a
# checkout carrying any of them still measures clean -- and the image would then ship
# uncommitted content under a claim of an exact commit. `artifacts/` is the sharpest
# case: it can hold support or audit evidence.
#
# Pinned as an invariant rather than a list by
# `test_no_ignored_path_can_enter_the_build_context`, so a future `.gitignore` entry
# cannot silently reopen this. The first fix here covered `.env` alone and left five
# other ignored paths; a list needs re-checking, an invariant does not.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
venv
ENV
artifacts
.idea
.vscode
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

.git
.github
.venv
__pycache__
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
htmlcov
.coverage*
output
lineage_data
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
tests
docs
*.md
